data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"The rank is k = ceil((n + 1)(1 - alpha)), where the n + 1 counts the test point. The threshold is the k-th smallest score. If k > n, no finite threshold exists and both bounds are infinite. Read alpha as the decimal it was written as (repr gives that text) and compute the rank with exact rational arithmetic, because a float product can round an exact integer up."},"hints_note":null}

